# Findings that are known, examined, and not secrets.
#
# A fingerprint is `commit:path:rule:line`, so an entry here exempts ONE
# finding in ONE commit. That is the point, and it is why this file is used
# rather than adding the value to `.gitleaks.toml`: an allowlist entry there
# would exempt the string everywhere, for ever, including somewhere it might
# one day mean something. A fingerprint cannot grow.
#
# Add a line only after reading the finding and establishing what the value is.
# "It is in a test" is not a reason — a real key pasted into a test file is
# still a real key.

